WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.300
This feature lived 17 minutes. So we asked it why it died.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.600
This is Exhume: a medium that runs Gemma 4 on your own laptop.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.520
First, plain code digs through git for everything that was deleted.

00:00:16.948 --> 00:00:21.728
Then we ask the dead. Gemma answers only from the evidence…

00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:25.688
…and cites it. E5 is the dead code's own comment.

00:00:26.918 --> 00:00:32.098
Dead websites come back from the Wayback Machine. Orkut quotes its own goodbye.

00:00:33.128 --> 00:00:37.588
For forgotten Mac apps, the date comes from macOS, not from the model.

00:00:39.107 --> 00:00:41.487
And when the evidence doesn't say…

00:00:43.273 --> 00:00:44.973
the spirits are silent.

00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:48.803
The whole story is at exhume.tech.

00:00:54.385 --> 00:00:57.405
Exhume. Open source, and free.

00:00:55.735 --> 00:00:58.235
exhume.tech · github.com/taseen-t/exhume
